;;; Syntax probe — rule-nary-and-or.
;;;
;;; A parametrised rule with a top-level `(or …)` over two
;;; disjuncts of different arity.
;;;
;;; Its `:assert` concluded `(quad ?d ?c ?b ?a)` until M1f S1f.5.10, which
;;; refuses a conclusion's variable a disjunct leaves unbound (F13): the
;;; second disjunct binds no `?c` or `?d`. It concludes what both bind since,
;;; and keeps its node kinds; no activator is written, so the rule never
;;; fires, before and after (Q-M1f.39).
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.

(rule n (?rel)
  :match  (or (quad ?a ?b ?c ?d) (?rel ?a ?b))
  :assert (quad ?b ?a ?b ?a))
